    careerPath: `Junior UX/UI Designer (80-130K, 0-2 года, working on features под supervision, learning Figma, building portfolio, mastering design basics) → Middle UX/UI Designer (150-280K, 2-4 года, owning projects end-to-end, conducting user research, working independently, collaborating с PM/dev) → Senior UX/UI Designer (320-400K+, 5-7 лет, leading initiatives, mentoring juniors, design system contributions, influencing product direction) → Lead Designer (400-500K, 7-10 лет, managing small team 2-4 designers, design process, cross-team projects) → Head of Design / Design Director (600K-1M+, 10+ лет, strategic design leadership, hiring, design culture, multiple products). Альтернативные пути: Product Designer (broader scope — не только UI, но и product strategy), UX Researcher (specialization в research), Design System Lead (focus на component libraries), Freelance Designer (independent work, variability income), Design Educator (курсы, workshops, content creation).`,
    responsibilities: [
      'User research — understanding user needs: conducting user interviews (1-on-1 moderated sessions, recording insights), creating surveys (Google Forms, Typeform), analyzing analytics (Amplitude/Mixpanel — user behavior patterns), competitive analysis (evaluating competitor products), creating personas (synthesizing research в user archetypes)',
      'Information architecture — проектирование structure: creating sitemaps (hierarchical page structure), designing user flows (visualizing journeys from entry → goal), navigation design (primary/secondary menus, breadcrumbs), organizing content (card sorting, taxonomy)',
      'Wireframing — low-fidelity layouts: sketching ideas (paper/whiteboard для rapid iteration), creating grayscale wireframes Figma (focusing на content hierarchy, not colors), annotating flows (explaining logic, interactions), exploring multiple concepts',
      'UI design — high-fidelity mockups: applying visual design (colors, typography, iconography), creating pixel-perfect layouts (consistent spacing, alignments), designing all states (default/hover/active/disabled/error/loading), ensuring responsive (mobile/tablet/desktop)',
      'Prototyping — interactive prototypes: linking screens Figma (creating clickable prototypes), adding transitions (smart animate, dissolve), designing micro-interactions (button press, form validation), creating high-fidelity prototypes для usability testing',
      'Usability testing — validating designs с users: writing test scenarios (tasks users должны complete), conducting moderated tests (observing users, taking notes), running unmoderated tests (Maze, UserTesting), analyzing results (identifying patterns, prioritizing issues)',
      'Design systems — creating and maintaining components: building UI component library (buttons, inputs, cards, modals), defining design tokens (colors, spacing, typography variables), writing documentation (usage guidelines, dos and donts), versioning (updating components across products)',
      'Collaboration с разработчиками — design handoff: creating specs (measurements, colors HEX/RGB, font sizes), exporting assets (@1x/@2x/@3x, SVG icons), using Figma inspect mode (auto-generating CSS/iOS/Android code), QA design implementation (checking если developers followed mockups)',
      'Работа с product team — alignment на goals: participating в planning meetings (understanding requirements, prioritizing features), presenting designs to stakeholders (explaining rationale, walking through flows), gathering feedback (iterating based on input), contributing to product strategy',
      'A/B testing & iteration — data-driven improvements: designing test variations (different button colors, CTAs, layouts), coordinating with analytics team (setting up experiments), analyzing results (statistical significance, conversion impact), iterating на winning designs',
      'Accessibility compliance — inclusive design: ensuring WCAG AA compliance (contrast ratios 4.5:1 for text, keyboard navigation), testing с screen readers (VoiceOver, NVDA), considering diverse abilities (color blindness, motor impairments), auditing designs (Stark plugin)',
      'Design critiques & reviews — improving team quality: participating в design reviews (giving constructive feedback), presenting own work для critique, learning from team (seeing different approaches), maintaining design quality standards',
      'Staying current — continuous learning: following design trends (Dribbble, Behance, Awwwards), reading design blogs (Nielsen Norman Group, Smashing Magazine, UX Collective), attending conferences/webinars (Awwwards, UX Moscow), experimenting с new tools/techniques',
    ],
