    howToBecome: `Путь в UX/UI дизайн один из most accessible в IT — не требуется programming background, можно войти через bootcamps или self-learning. Realistic timeline: 6-12 месяцев intensive learning + portfolio building.

**Phase 1: Design Fundamentals (1-2 месяца).** Изучите основы визуального дизайна: color theory (complementary/analogous colors, 60-30-10 rule, accessibility contrast WCAG), typography (font pairing — serif+sans-serif, hierarchy H1/H2/Body, line-height 1.5, letter-spacing), composition (visual hierarchy, balance, alignment, white space), Gestalt principles (proximity, similarity, closure — how humans perceive visual information). Ресурсы: "The Design of Everyday Things" (Don Norman — UX bible), "Don't Make Me Think" (Steve Krug — web usability), Refactoring UI book (practical UI tips), YouTube каналы (Flux, Jesse Showalter). Practice: redesign существующих apps (Dribbble rebound challenges), analyze good design (why does this work?).

**Phase 2: Learn Figma (2-3 месяца intensive).** Figma — mandatory tool (80% вакансий требуют). Освойте: interface basics (frames, layers, groups), vector tools (pen tool, boolean operations, масками), auto-layout (responsive design without manual resizing), components (creating reusable elements, variants для states), prototyping (linking screens, transitions, overlays), collaboration (sharing files, commenting, version history). Ресурсы: Figma official tutorials (free, comprehensive), Figma Community (free templates/plugins), YouTube (DesignCourse, Femke, Caler Edwards практические tutorials). Practice: recreate popular app screens (Instagram, Airbnb, Spotify — pixel-perfect reproduction учит attention to detail).

**Phase 3: UX Process & Research (2-3 месяца).** Изучите UX methodology: Design Thinking process (empathize → define → ideate → prototype → test), user research methods (interviews, surveys, usability testing), creating personas (synthesizing research в user archetypes), user journey mapping (visualizing experience over time), information architecture (sitemaps, user flows, card sorting), wireframing (low-fi before high-fi — avoid premature visual design). Ресурсы: Nielsen Norman Group articles (gold standard UX research), Interaction Design Foundation courses ($14/month, comprehensive), "Sprint" book (Jake Knapp — Google design sprint methodology), Laws of UX website (psychological principles). Practice: conduct user interviews с friends/family (о любом product), create user flows для daily tasks (ordering coffee, booking flight).

**Phase 4: Build Portfolio (3-4 месяца — most critical).** Portfolio важнее degree для hiring. Create 3-5 case studies showcasing process (not just final designs): Personal project (redesigning app you use daily — explain pain points, research, iterations), Course project (if doing bootcamp — usually capstone project), Volunteer work (nonprofits need design help — real client, real constraints), Unsolicited redesigns (but show process, не только pretty screens). Structure case studies: Problem statement → Research (user interviews, competitive analysis) → Ideation (sketches, wireframes) → Visual design (high-fi mockups) → Prototype → Testing (if possible) → Results/learnings. Host portfolio на: Behance (industry standard), personal website (shows extra effort — use Webflow, Framer, Readymag templates), Figma Community (показывая working files). Important: show YOUR thinking process, не just beautiful final designs (recruiters want to see how you solve problems).

**Phase 5: Специализация & Advanced Skills (2-3 месяца параллельно).** Deepen expertise: Design systems (Atomic Design methodology, creating component libraries, documentation), accessibility (WCAG guidelines, testing с screen readers, inclusive design), interaction design (micro-interactions, animations, prototyping advanced tools like Framer/ProtoPie), front-end basics (HTML/CSS fundamentals — not coding, но understanding constraints), analytics (Google Analytics basics, understanding metrics — conversion, bounce rate, engagement). Рассмотрите niche specialization: Mobile design (iOS Human Interface Guidelines, Material Design), Design systems, UX research, Accessibility specialist.

**Phase 6: Bootcamp or Self-Learning Decision.** Bootcamps (Яндекс.Практикум Designer ~80-120K₽, Skillbox/Netology ~60-100K₽, international — Designlab, CareerFoundry $5-7K) provide: structured curriculum, mentorship, networking, job placement помощь, portfolio projects, credential (certificate). Self-learning (free or cheap): более гибко, дешевле, но requires discipline, no networking, harder breaking in without credential. Recommendation: если можете afford bootcamp и need structure — worth investment; если budget-conscious и self-motivated — self-learning + portfolio достаточно.

**Phase 7: Job Search & Networking (1-2 месяца).** Prepare для job search: polish portfolio (quality over quantity — 3 great case studies лучше 10 mediocre), update LinkedIn (design role, portfolio link), practice presenting designs (storytelling, explaining rationale), prepare для interviews (whiteboard challenges — design process, portfolio walkthrough). Where to apply: job boards (hh.ru, LinkedIn, Behance job listings), company websites directly (check careers pages Яндекс/Ozon/Тинькофф), networking (Telegram design chats, meetups — Moscow Design Community, UX Russia), referrals (reach out designers LinkedIn, informational interviews). Interview process typically: portfolio review → design task (take-home 3-7 days — redesign feature or solve problem) → presentation (walkthrough решение, explaining process) → culture fit. Junior positions competitive, но consistent applications + portfolio improvements → offers.

**Realistic timeline:** 6-12 месяцев full-time equivalent (4-6 часов/день), faster если already имеете related skills (graphic design, marketing), slower если part-time learning. Costs: bootcamp $1500-7000 (optional), Figma free, books/courses $100-300, total investment primarily time.`,
