    careerPath: `Типичный путь в UX research: Junior UX Researcher (0-2 года, conducting research под supervision Senior UXR, 1-2 studies per quarter, learning research methods) → UX Researcher / Middle UXR (2-4 года, owning research projects end-to-end, 3-5 studies per quarter, working independently, starting to mentor juniors) → Senior UX Researcher (4-7 лет, leading complex multi-method studies, strategic research planning, mentoring team, influencing product roadmap) → Lead UX Researcher (7-10+ лет, managing 2-4 researchers, setting research standards, stakeholder management на уровне Directors/VPs) → Principal UX Researcher (10-15+ лет, thought leadership, cross-product research initiatives, building research culture) или Head of User Research / Research Manager (managing research teams 5-20 people, hiring, process development, research operations). Альтернативные треки: переход в Product Management (user-centric PM), Design Research (embedded в design teams), UX Strategy Consultant, founding research agencies.

Рост зависит от portfolio сильных исследований (case studies demonstrating impact), presentation skills (убедительные research readouts для stakeholders), influence на product decisions (tracking how research insights изменили roadmap). Senior+ UX Researchers часто publish thought leadership (Medium articles, conference talks at UXPA, ResearchOps Community), contribute to research community (mentoring, workshops). Lead/Principal роли требуют strong stakeholder management и ability to scale research practices across large organizations.`,
