        'Visual Creativity — seeing motion potential: imagining how static designs could move, creating unexpected delightful moments (Easter eggs, playful interactions), translating brand personality в motion language',
        'Technical Problem-Solving — working within constraints: finding creative solutions when Lottie doesnt support feature, optimizing performance without sacrificing visual quality, balancing file size plus richness',
        'Communication and Collaboration — cross-functional work: explaining motion decisions to non-animators (why this timing, why this easing), translating UX/UI designer intent в motion, collaborating with engineers на implementation',
        'Adaptability and Learning — keeping current: learning new tools rapidly (Rive, Haiku, новые Lottie features), adapting to emerging platforms (AR/VR motion patterns, wearables constraints), experimenting with techniques',
        'Storytelling through Motion — narrative thinking: using animation to guide attention, creating emotional resonance через movement pacing, building narrative arcs в onboarding flows',
        'Self-Criticism and Quality Standards — pushing excellence: never settling for "good enough" timing, constantly comparing against best-in-class examples (Stripe, Apple, Google animations), maintaining high bar',
