    careerPath: `Типичный путь в 3D Design: Junior 3D Designer (0-2 года, creating simple 3D assets под supervision, learning software basics, practicing modeling/texturing, building portfolio) → 3D Designer / Middle (2-4 года, owning asset creation independently, photorealistic product renders, web3D implementation, mentoring juniors) → Senior 3D Designer (4-7 лет, complex projects: full environments, character modeling, advanced materials, setting quality standards) → Lead 3D Designer (7-10 plus лет, managing 3D team 2-5 people, art direction, pipeline development, cross-project consistency) или Technical Artist (bridging 3D art + development, optimizing workflows, shader development) или Art Director (creative leadership beyond just 3D, visual direction).

Альтернативные треки: 3D Designer → Game Artist (specializing в game assets, real-time optimization, Unity/Unreal workflows), Architectural Visualizer (archviz focus, V-Ray/Corona rendering, photorealistic interiors/exteriors), Motion Graphics Artist (3D animation emphasis, Cinema 4D specialization, broadcast design), VR/AR Developer (technical 3D, coding skills, Unity/Unreal development), Product Designer (3D as differentiator, industrial design crossover), Creative Technologist (code-based 3D, Three.js/WebGL expertise).

Рост зависит от: portfolio quality (showreel демонстрирующий range: products, environments, characters, 60-90 seconds), technical mastery (advanced modeling topology, shader complexity, render optimization), understanding business context (e-commerce needs, performance budgets, platform constraints), specialization (becoming expert в niche: product viz, AR, characters).`,
